nce of congenital hypothyroidism in Quebec.", "VAN VLIET G:Van Vliet G is an author recognized for contributions to the field of paediatric endocrinology, particularly in relation to congenital hypothyroidism. They are one of the authors of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism, which provides important recommendations and standards for the diagnosis and management of this condition. Additionally, Van Vliet G has co-authored a study examining the incidence of congenital hypothyroidism in Quebec, further contributing to the understanding and research surrounding this endocrine disorder.", "J CLIN ENDOCRINOL METAB:The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism (J Clin Endocrinol Metab) is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research and clinical practice guidelines related to endocrinology and metabolism. It features a wide range of studies, including those focused on adrenal insufficiency, hyponatremia, congenital hypothyroidism, thyroid disease, and conditions such as pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma. The journal has also published significant clinical practice guidelines on endocrine treatment for gender-dysphoric individuals, as well as research on the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIAD) and glucocorticoid deficiency. Overall, J Clin Endocrinol Metab serves as a vital resource for advancements in the field of endocrinology.", "LAFRANCHI SH:LaFranchi SH is an author recognized for contributions to the field of neonatal health, specifically focusing on the diagnosis and treatment of neonatal hypothyroidism. Their work includes significant studies that explore various aspects of this condition, providing valuable insights into effective management and therapeutic approaches.", "LEGERS J:Leger J is an author of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism.", "HORM RES PEDIATR:Horm Res Pediatr is the journal where the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines were published.", "RODRIGUEZ A:Rodríguez A is an author who wrote about neonatal screening in endocrine diseases.", "REV ESP ENDOCRINOL PEDIATR:Rev Esp Endocrinol Pediatr is the journal where the article on neonatal screening in endocrine diseases was published.", "DEFECTOS EN LA SÍNTESIS DE HORMONAS TIROIDEAS:Defects in the synthesis of thyroid hormones are the second most common cause of congenital hypothyroidism, explaining 10% to 15% of cases.", "ANTICUERPOS BLOQUEANTES DEL RECEPTOR DE LA TSH:Maternal transfer of blocking antibodies to the TSH receptor can cause transient congenital hypothyroidism.", "LITIO:LITIO, or lithium, is a medication primarily used as a mood stabilizer in the treatment of mood disorders. It is known to affect various physiological processes in the body. One significant effect of lithium is its potential to alter calcium levels, leading to conditions such as hypercalcemia. Additionally, the excretion of lithium is influenced by sodium intake, which can impact its effectiveness and safety.\n\nLithium is also associated with several side effects, including the development of primary hypothyroidism in up to 20% of patients undergoing treatment. Another notable side effect is nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, which can occur in some individuals taking the medication. Overall, while lithium is an effective treatment for mood disorders, it requires careful monitoring due to its various effects on the body and potential side effects.", "AMIODARONA:Amiodarona is an antiarrhythmic medication that is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. This drug is notable for its high iodine content, which can lead to thyroid dysfunction in approximately 15-20% of patients. Specifically, amiodarona can induce both hyperthyroidism and hypothyroidism, particularly in individuals with pre-existing thyroiditis. The risk of hypothyroidism is especially pronounced in regions where there is a low intake of iodine. Overall, amiodarona is a significant medication in the management of arrhythmias, but it carries the potential for thyroid-related side effects that require monitoring."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}